# 9. `size()`

## LEVEL 1

`size()` returns the number of elements present in the collection.

```java
c.size();
```

---

## LEVEL 2

If:

```text
[10, 20, 30]
```

then:

```java
c.size();
```

returns:

```text
3
```

---

## LEVEL 3 — Program

```java
import java.util.*;

class Demo
{
    public static void main(String[] args)
    {
        Collection c = new ArrayList();

        c.add(10);
        c.add(20);
        c.add(30);

        System.out.println(c.size());
    }
}
```

Output:

```text
3
```

Return type:

```text
