# 10. `isEmpty()`

## LEVEL 1

`isEmpty()` checks whether the collection contains zero elements.

---

## LEVEL 2

Empty collection:

```text
[]
```

```java
c.isEmpty();
```

returns:

```text
true
```

Non-empty collection:

```text
[10]
```

returns:

```text
false
```

---

## LEVEL 3 — Program

```java
import java.util.*;

class Demo
{
    public static void main(String[] args)
    {
        Collection c = new ArrayList();

        System.out.println(c.isEmpty());

        c.add(10);

        System.out.println(c.isEmpty());
    }
}
```

Output:

```text
true
false
```

### Remember

```text
size()
    ↓
How many?

isEmpty()
    ↓
Are there ZERO?
```

