# 🔥 3LEVEL MASTER TABLE

| Method          | LEVEL 1 Meaning          | LEVEL 2                            | LEVEL 3              |
| --------------- | ------------------------ | ---------------------------------- | -------------------- |
| `add()`         | Add element              | One element                        | `c.add(10)`          |
| `addAll()`      | Add collection elements  | Collection → collection            | `c1.addAll(c2)`      |
| `remove()`      | Remove element           | Matching element                   | `c.remove(10)`       |
| `removeAll()`   | Remove matching elements | Based on another collection        | `c1.removeAll(c2)`   |
| `contains()`    | Search                   | One element                        | `c.contains(10)`     |
| `containsAll()` | Search multiple          | All elements of another collection | `c1.containsAll(c2)` |
| `size()`        | Count                    | Number of elements                 | `c.size()`           |
| `isEmpty()`     | Empty check              | Zero elements?                     | `c.isEmpty()`        |
| `clear()`       | Empty collection         | Remove everything                  | `c.clear()`          |
| `iterator()`    | Traverse                 | Obtain Iterator                    | `c.iterator()`       |
| `toArray()`     | Convert                  | Collection → array                 | `c.toArray()`        |

---

# 🧠 The Ultimate 3-Level Memory Map

```text
                 COLLECTION
                     │
       ┌─────────────┼──────────────┐
       │             │              │
      ADD          REMOVE         SEARCH
       │             │              │
   add()         remove()       contains()
   addAll()      removeAll()    containsAll()
                     │
                   clear()
       │
       └─────────────┬──────────────┐
                     │              │
                 INFORMATION       OTHER
                     │              │
                 size()         iterator()
                 isEmpty()      toArray()
```

## One-line revision

```text
add       → add ONE
addAll    → add MANY
remove    → remove ONE
removeAll → remove MATCHING
contains  → check ONE
containsAll → check ALL
size      → COUNT
isEmpty   → ZERO?
clear     → REMOVE EVERYTHING
iterator  → TRAVERSE
toArray   → CONVERT TO ARRAY
```

### The key foundation

If you can look at a collection and immediately decide:

```text
"I want to add"       → add()
"I want to add many"  → addAll()

"I want to remove"    → remove()
"I want to remove matching groups" → removeAll()

"I want to search one" → contains()
"I want to search all" → containsAll()

"I want the count"    → size()
"I want to check zero" → isEmpty()

"I want everything gone" → clear()

"I want to traverse"  → iterator()

"I want an array"     → toArray()
```

then you have the **Collection Interface foundation** required before moving into `List`, `Set`, and `Queue`.
